# DocMind Frontend — Clean Architecture

## Styling

- **No inline styles.** Do not use `style={{ }}` or the `style` prop.
- **Tailwind only.** Use Tailwind utility classes for all styling. No CSS modules, no styled-components, no global CSS beyond `src/index.css` Tailwind directives.
- Keep `index.css` limited to `@tailwind base;`, `@tailwind components;`, `@tailwind utilities;` unless explicitly extending with design tokens.

## Components

- **Reusable components.** Extract repeated UI into `components/ui/` (buttons, inputs, cards, etc.) and layout into `components/layout/`.
- **Small and modular.** One clear responsibility per component. Split large components into smaller ones.
- **Composition.** Prefer composition over large prop lists. Use `children` and slot-style props where appropriate.

## Structure

- **Pages** in `src/pages/` — one file per route/screen; pages compose layout and feature components.
- **Features** in `src/features/` — feature-specific components and logic.
- **Routes** in `src/routes/` — route definitions and guards.
- **Services** in `src/services/` — API calls (e.g. axios), no UI.
- **Hooks** in `src/hooks/` — shared state and side-effect logic.

## Examples

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — inline style
<div style={{ padding: 16, backgroundColor: '#fff' }}>

// ✅ GOOD — Tailwind
<div className="p-4 bg-white">

// ❌ BAD — giant single component
// ✅ GOOD — small components composed in a page
```
